```suggestion
        ParsedSettings parentSettings;
        ParsedSettings childSettings;
```
Would it be possible to rename it to something like this? That way, if we ever want to add a chain of layers, we can reuse this?

Yeah I found it extremely annoying as well, so I fixed the if condition at some point. It'll now check the length of the URI early:
```cpp
// Anything longer than 2 wchar_t's _isn't_ an emoji or symbol,
// so treat it as an invalid path.
if (const auto icon = profile.Icon(); icon.size() > 2)
```

After all, a path with environment variable is _at least_ 3 characters long (`%x%`).
And if we treat all arguments with a length of 2 or less as an emoji, then we don't need to check for the validity of the URI in the first place.

